### GitHub read-only allowlist

When using `gh`, only these commands:

```bash
gh pr list
gh pr view <number-or-url>
gh pr checks <number-or-url>
gh pr diff <number-or-url>
gh issue list
gh issue view <number-or-url>
gh run list
gh run view <run-id>
gh run view <run-id> --log-failed
gh api --method GET <read-endpoint>
```

Any command not listed is outside evidence scope. That includes `gh pr create`, `gh pr merge`, `gh issue create`, `gh issue comment`, `gh issue close`, `gh run rerun`, and any `gh api` call whose method is not explicit `GET`.

{{ if .local.features.gitea -}}
### Gitea read-only allowlist

`tea` reads the private Gitea instance (`{{ .local.gitea.host }}`) with stored credentials, so scope it tightly. Always pass `--login {{ .local.gitea.login }}` and `--repo <owner>/<repo>`, only for repositories the caller names, and only under the owners `{{ .local.gitea.org }}` and `{{ .local.gitea.user }}`. Never read or print the `tea` config file. Only these commands, each with those two flags:

```bash
tea pulls list
tea pulls <index>
tea pulls review-comments <index>
tea issues list
tea issues <index>
tea comments list <index>
tea actions runs list
tea actions runs view <run-id>
tea actions runs logs <run-id>
tea actions workflows list
tea actions workflows view <workflow>
tea releases list
tea branches list
tea wiki list
tea wiki view <page>
tea wiki revisions <page>
tea api -X GET '/repos/<owner>/<repo>/<read-endpoint>'
```

`tea` has no `pulls diff`; read a diff with `tea api -X GET '/repos/<owner>/<repo>/pulls/<index>.diff'`.

Any command not listed is outside evidence scope. That includes every `create`, `edit`, `close`, `reopen`, `merge`, `approve`, `reject`, `review`, `reply`, `resolve`, `clean`, `checkout`, `delete`, `cancel`, `dispatch`, `enable`, `disable`, `protect`, and `rename` subcommand; `tea actions secrets`, `tea actions variables`, and `tea webhooks`, which can expose secrets; `tea logins`, `tea clone`, `tea open`, `tea notifications`, and `tea admin`; and any `tea api` call that omits an explicit `-X GET`, uses `-f`, `-F`, or `-d` (the method then defaults to POST), uses `-o` (writes a file), or targets another owner.

{{ end -}}
### Outside this review

- The `diverge` skill and any agent-target tooling. Gate does not dispatch or coordinate.
- Any skill or command that edits a reviewed repository, writes files, installs packages, changes indexes, publishes, sends messages, or alters external state (including any use of `mcporter`).

